      "observed": "On the Power Train sheet D3 is drawn as a 12 V TVS/Zener from the +24V input node (after F1) to GND, in parallel with the 28 V input TVS D2.",
      "expected": "The 24 V input is specified to be clamped by the 28 V TVS D2; a 12 V clamp placed directly across the 24 V rail would break down continuously and is inconsistent with a 24 V input rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "F1 (fuse) ─► D2 (TVS clamp) ─► /+24V_FB  ──► +24V bulk rail"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Power Train sheet: 'D2 28V' and 'D3 12V' both drawn from the +24V input node down to the GND symbol"}
      ],
      "impact": "If D3 is a rail clamp rather than a gate-protection clamp, it would conduct continuously on the 24 V rail, dragging the rail toward ~12 V and preventing the board from powering up (TVS destroyed or the 24 V supply current-limited).",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing largely matches the specification (I2C pull-ups 2.2k, 110 mΩ sense resistors, 100 Ω gate and 4.7 kΩ interlock resistors, ADM3260 isolation, TMC2209 wiring all agree), but the ATO_VALVE net is wired to the ESP32-C6's IO7/SPI_MOSI pin instead of the IO2 pin the specification's pin cross-check table lists, and a 12 V TVS (D3) appears placed across the 24 V input rail."
}

